shell scripting
******************************************************
Shell scripting is the native linux scripting. 
---> A Shell is a program that takes your commands and tells Linux to execute them. 
---> If you keep all your linux commands in a single file and execute that file is called shell scripting.
---> It is used to automate the manual process.
---> Shell scripting is used to fetch the information from linux servers.
Syntax:
=============
#!/bin/bash
echo “hello world”
save as “filename.sh”
#!/bin/bash ---> It should be the first line in shell script. It can be called as “shebang” used to interpret and execute the commands and syntax inside shell script.
In shell script, we use “ Datatypes, Variables, Functions, Loops, conditions “ to enhance the script.
Some special variables used in shell script are:
*****************************************
$@ : All variables passed
$# : No of variables
$0 : script name
$pwd : Present working directory
$Home : Home directory of current user
$USER : Which user is running the script
$$ : process id of current script
$! : Process id of last command in background
$? : exit status, 0 -> success , other than “0” --> failure
Datatypes:
*************
Integer : number, Float : decimals, Boolean : True/false, String : Text,
Array : [“name1” “name 2” “name 3”], map : name: value, name2: value
operators used in conditions:
*****************************
-eq :equal
-ne : not equal
-gt : greater than
-lt : Less than
-ge : greater or equal
-le : less or equal
